<h2>What is Correspondence Chess?</h2>

<p>
Correspondence chess is chess played over distance.
Historically, moves were exchanged by postcard and letter,
often resulting in games lasting many months or even years.
Today most correspondence chess is played on dedicated
internet servers while preserving the same spirit of deep
analysis and careful planning.
</p>

<p>
Unlike ordinary tournament chess, players may spend several
days analysing a single position. This makes correspondence
chess a unique blend of practical play, research and chess
history.
</p>

<p>
Norway has a proud tradition in correspondence chess through
the Norwegian Correspondence Chess Federation founded in 1945.
</p>

