<h2>About Arild Haugen</h2>

<p>
My interest in chess began in Stavanger during the 1950s when
my father, the Norwegian magician Ramiras, introduced me to
the game.
</p>

<p>
What started as a childhood hobby developed into decades of
tournament chess, correspondence chess, analysis and chess
history. Through the years I have represented Norway in
international correspondence events and participated in
numerous ICCF competitions.
</p>

<p>
These pages contain selected games, articles, photographs,
historical material and memories collected throughout a
lifetime in chess.
</p>

